course: dictionary
lesson: 7399
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word pod is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it: they are its context. «A bean plant grows seeds, then pods with new seeds.» Here a pod is the long case that holds seeds, because that is what the words around it are about.
explain: Now read this: «A pod of dolphins swam past the boat.» A pod is not a seed case here. The clues are dolphins and swam, so a pod must be a group of animals swimming together. Try your meaning in the sentence: a group of dolphins swam past the boat. It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Sometimes the meaning is a small separate part. «The astronaut jumped into the escape pod.» An escape pod is a small capsule that can carry people away from danger. When you meet a word with more than one meaning, ask: which meaning fits these words best?
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: Pod has three main meanings: a seed case, a group of whales, dolphins or seals, and a small separate capsule.
fact: «Pea pod» means the long case that holds peas.
fact: «A pod of dolphins» means a group of dolphins swimming together.
fact: «Escape pod» means a small capsule that carries people away from danger, as in stories about space ships.
exercise: «Some seeds are shot out when the pod bursts open, like peas.» What is a pod in this sentence? | *A seed case | A group of dolphins | A small plant | A space capsule
exercise: «A pod of dolphins swam past the boat.» What is a pod in this sentence? | A kind of boat | *A group swimming together | An escape capsule | A long case for seeds
exercise: Find and copy one word from «A bean plant's life cycle is seed, seedling, adult plant with flowers, and pods with new seeds.» that names a young plant. | *seedling | adult | cycle | flowers
test: «The astronaut jumped into the escape pod.» In this sentence, pod means | A group of whales | A long case that holds seeds | *A small separate capsule | A kind of coat
test: Which phrase uses pod to mean a seed case? | a coffee pod | *pea pod | escape pod | a pod of seals
exam: Pod has more than one meaning, and you are not sure which one fits. What should you do? | Skip the sentence and never read it again | Ask someone to remove the word from the text | *Read the words around it and try each meaning in the sentence | Guess the first meaning you think of and never check
